From b1957fc88df8a9f2d3a1dab579ff8a570d0c36b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:13:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] fix: resolve fullScene guard contradictions and toast
 stacking (audit items 1-4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Prompt contradiction fixed — fullScene:false now only applies when the item
   cannot be identified at all (blank/blurred/fragment). Room shots and close-ups
   that still show a recognisable item pass. The ≥85%-of-frame instruction no
   longer conflicts with the guard.

2. Toast overwrite fixed — TOAST_LIMIT raised 1→3 so the per-photo rejection
   toast is never silenced by the generic success/failure toast that fires after.

3. Photos preserved on rejection — needsReplacement photos stay in the upload
   grid (customer can replace them). They are removed from analyzedUrls so
   uploading a replacement re-triggers analysis. They are excluded from the
   identified-items list since they carry no usable data.

4. fullScene:false results excluded from both vision caches — the throw happens
   before visionResultCache.set / visionHashCache.set, so a retry with a better
   photo is always possible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QZJ9qadsGiEeGDBZCsxhZ
