 motorcycle vehicle tier
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Remove three `maxDbTier` blocks in RequestMove.tsx that were forcing
  vehicle class up to the highest per-item `vehicleType` from the DB.
  A single sofa tagged `vehicle: 'van'` was overriding the volume-based
  calculation for the whole load, causing a 104 ft³ job to be quoted as
  Cargo Van instead of Pickup Truck.
- Vehicle class is now determined purely by volume thresholds:
  ≤54 ft³ → SUV, ≤136 ft³ → Pickup Truck, ≤318 ft³ → Cargo Van, else Moving Truck.
- Correct motorcycle (standard/cruiser) from `vehicle: 'van'` to `vehicle: 'pickup'`
  (68 ft³, well within the 136 ft³ Pickup threshold).
- All other `vehicle: 'van'` and `vehicle: 'truck'` items were audited and
  confirmed correct by volume (sectionals >136 ft³) or weight (pianos, hot tubs,
  safes, pool tables all >250 kg legitimately requiring a truck).

